WEBVTT

00:04.052 --> 00:05.928
What was it?

00:06.262 --> 00:07.221
Ever since last night,

00:07.305 --> 00:10.558
I've had this feeling
I'm supposed to do something…

00:11.392 --> 00:15.892
Boy, my shoes and bag
sure feel heavy today.

00:16.481 --> 00:17.231
Huh?

00:18.942 --> 00:20.777
<i>Th-This house…</i>

00:21.319 --> 00:22.320
<i>Why?</i>

00:22.695 --> 00:26.490
<i>Somehow I ended up
walking to Rohan-Sensei's house.</i>

00:28.117 --> 00:29.493
<i>The door's open…</i>

00:30.078 --> 00:32.872
<i>I'd like to drop in and
thank him for yesterday,</i>

00:33.206 --> 00:37.627
<i>but I'll be late for school.
I probably shouldn't.</i>

00:38.253 --> 00:40.546
<i>Being a manga artist,
he's probably still asleep.</i>

00:41.256 --> 00:43.508
<i>I really shouldn't just barge in.</i>

00:44.259 --> 00:45.510
<i>This really isn't
such a good idea…</i>

00:54.769 --> 00:56.437
<i>Rohan-sensei..</i>

00:57.272 --> 00:59.816
<i>He's working with
such a chilling expression.</i>

01:00.191 --> 01:01.192
<i>What is this…</i>

01:01.776 --> 01:05.321
<i>I can't shake the feeling that
being here is actually terrifying.</i>

01:05.405 --> 01:06.572
<i>What is it?</i>

01:07.282 --> 01:08.533
So you made it.

01:08.950 --> 01:09.951
I've been waiting.

01:10.493 --> 01:11.535
You're right on time.

01:11.953 --> 01:12.745
Huh?

01:12.829 --> 01:16.332
Forgive me, but could I
ask you to wait for a moment?

01:16.624 --> 01:17.499
Just two more pages,

01:17.584 --> 01:19.836
and next week's manuscript
will be complete.

01:20.795 --> 01:22.797
It'll only take about
twenty minutes.

01:23.256 --> 01:24.298
<i>Twenty minutes?</i>

01:24.507 --> 01:27.259
<i>Did he just say
two pages in twenty minutes?</i>

01:27.468 --> 01:28.677
<i>I must've misheard him.</i>

01:28.970 --> 01:31.389
<i>Two pages in twenty minutes
from scratch?</i>

01:31.472 --> 01:34.224
<i>That'd be impossible…
And next week's?</i>

01:34.642 --> 01:36.977
<i>He just showed us yesterday
this week's manuscript,</i>

01:37.061 --> 01:38.729
<i>and he'd just finished it.</i>

01:49.907 --> 01:52.618
What?! Straight to pen?!

01:55.955 --> 01:57.706
I-I don't believe it…

01:57.832 --> 02:00.793
Such complex composition,
and without any sketching!

02:00.918 --> 02:02.419
He's hammering it out
with no hesitation…

02:02.503 --> 02:05.422
And with the backgrounds!

02:17.518 --> 02:19.186
W-What was that?!

02:19.395 --> 02:21.688
I didn't get a good look.
What'd he just do?!

02:25.610 --> 02:28.112
What?! "Beta" coloring?!

02:28.196 --> 02:29.780
He's flicking the ink around
like shurikens,

02:29.864 --> 02:32.575
with perfect precision
and not a single stray mark!

02:32.700 --> 02:34.159
Th-That technique…

02:34.243 --> 02:38.247
Isn't beta coloring done
with a brush?!

02:39.999 --> 02:41.083
BOOM

02:41.459 --> 02:43.586
The beta coloring's already done!

02:44.045 --> 02:47.256
It took him only
about two minutes, start to finish!

02:48.424 --> 02:50.592
All thanks to you, Koichi.

02:50.843 --> 02:52.845
My creative urges runneth over!

02:53.054 --> 02:54.722
My appetite to draw is insatiable!

02:54.931 --> 02:56.140
I want to draw more!

02:56.224 --> 02:58.142
Drawing nineteen pages in one night

02:58.226 --> 03:00.603
is something I've
never ever experienced before!

03:01.145 --> 03:04.106
At this very moment,
a masterpiece is being born!

03:04.565 --> 03:05.941
Your life experiences
are astonishing!

03:06.192 --> 03:08.277
- Huh?
- I'm basing my story

03:08.361 --> 03:10.321
- What…?
- on your experience, Koichi!

03:14.951 --> 03:18.204
Get cracking!
I want your next reality!

03:18.287 --> 03:19.830
Show me your next page!

03:20.123 --> 03:23.334
Your weight decreases with
every page I take,

03:23.418 --> 03:24.794
but you don't mind, right?

03:25.086 --> 03:29.586
For you will become a masterpiece,
immortalized for all eternity!

03:32.427 --> 03:33.177
FLIP

03:33.261 --> 03:34.011
Now I remember!

03:34.595 --> 03:36.388
Heaven's Door!

03:36.514 --> 03:40.684
Y-You're a Stand user!

04:00.121 --> 04:00.704
JOJO'S BIZARRE ADVENTURE
DIAMOND IS UNBREAKABLE

04:00.788 --> 04:02.915
<i>A demon's crept into
our everyday life</i>

04:02.999 --> 04:05.292
<i>It's about to take away
something precious</i>

04:05.376 --> 04:08.629
<i>Our peace has already
crumbled long ago</i>

04:09.380 --> 04:11.465
<i>So casually, so nonchalantly</i>

04:11.549 --> 04:13.884
<i>It's taken from us
before we know it</i>

04:13.968 --> 04:17.179
<i>If we want it back,
now's the chance</i>

04:17.430 --> 04:20.933
<i>With the sharpness of
the piercing arrow</i>

04:21.726 --> 04:25.104
<i>The beauty of two souls united</i>

04:25.188 --> 04:27.773
<i>Wherever you go, chase you</i>

04:27.857 --> 04:29.984
<i>Whenever, chase you</i>

04:30.067 --> 04:32.069
<i>I will chase you</i>

04:32.153 --> 04:33.737
<i>Nowhere to escape</i>

04:33.821 --> 04:36.406
<i>Start running, I will chase you</i>

04:36.491 --> 04:38.493
<i>Tomorrow, chase you</i>

04:38.576 --> 04:41.287
<i>My fists will be the one
to show you</i>

04:41.496 --> 04:45.996
<i>Tenacity decides
who will win or lose</i>

04:47.168 --> 04:51.668
<i>So I chase you</i>

04:56.010 --> 04:57.177
Look…

04:56.302 --> 05:00.802
EPISODE 15
LET'S GO TO
THE MANGA ARTIST'S HOUSE, PART 2

04:57.261 --> 04:58.929
It's not even done yet,

04:59.013 --> 05:00.911
and this single panel
could be a book in and of itself!

05:01.557 --> 05:02.724
This is amazing!

05:02.809 --> 05:06.771
I'm maturing…
as a manga artist and a Stand user!

05:06.938 --> 05:09.065
Now if you don't mind,
Koichi, I'm going to read this.

05:17.657 --> 05:18.824
Interesting…

05:19.075 --> 05:20.076
If I'm not mistaken,

05:20.159 --> 05:22.452
those are the faces of
Shining Diamond's Josuke Higashikata

05:22.954 --> 05:25.539
and The Hand's Okuyasu Nijimura.

05:26.207 --> 05:27.708
But good heavens…

05:28.042 --> 05:31.003
Why are they coming to my house?

05:31.254 --> 05:34.298
There's no way Koichi
would've mentioned me to those two.

05:35.424 --> 05:36.466
How peculiar…

05:38.302 --> 05:39.177
Huh?

05:40.471 --> 05:43.390
I-It's Josuke and Okuyasu!

05:43.474 --> 05:46.852
I have no idea how
they found me here, but…

05:49.438 --> 05:52.774
I've got to get them to save me!
Somehow!

05:54.694 --> 05:55.903
Somehow…

05:56.195 --> 05:59.781
I have to get them to save me!

06:02.034 --> 06:05.328
Huh? Okuyasu and Josuke?

06:05.413 --> 06:07.581
How did you know I was here?

06:11.878 --> 06:12.920
Now, then…

06:13.212 --> 06:16.298
For now, Josuke and
Okuyasu are of no interest to me.

06:17.049 --> 06:20.052
I'll finish up the last
two pages for next week,

06:20.511 --> 06:23.639
and seize even more material
from Koichi!

06:24.932 --> 06:26.475
I can hardly contain myself!

06:26.559 --> 06:29.853
Huh? You were watching
a manga artist at work?

06:29.937 --> 06:32.898
This is where he works?

06:32.982 --> 06:34.358
Rohan Kishibe?

06:34.442 --> 06:36.152
Is he famous or something?

06:36.444 --> 06:38.154
Ever heard of him, Josuke?

06:38.529 --> 06:40.739
Nah. Remember,
even that bastard Hazamada

06:40.823 --> 06:43.659
gave me a hard time for not
knowing what Perman was.

06:44.118 --> 06:45.410
<i>That wasn't it.</i>

06:45.494 --> 06:49.039
<i>That wasn't what I wanted
to say to them.</i>

06:49.123 --> 06:51.041
<i>But what was it?</i>

06:51.334 --> 06:53.919
Well, you were staggering around

06:54.003 --> 06:55.587
so we thought we better tail you,

06:55.838 --> 06:57.923
but if everything's
hunky dory, then all right.

06:58.507 --> 06:59.758
Nothing to worry about.

06:59.967 --> 07:00.884
Thanks.

07:00.968 --> 07:03.303
Aren't you gonna come in
and observe with me?

07:03.429 --> 07:04.972
Nah, I'll pass.

07:05.389 --> 07:07.849
Famous people make me nervous.

07:08.225 --> 07:09.226
Same here.

07:09.352 --> 07:13.852
Knowing you weren't with some chick
is enough for me.

07:15.191 --> 07:16.483
See ya, Koichi.

07:16.776 --> 07:17.777
Bye.

07:20.321 --> 07:22.531
<i>I'm drawing a blank.</i>

07:22.823 --> 07:26.701
<i>I know I meant to tell
them something really important.</i>

07:28.996 --> 07:30.872
I remember now!

07:31.040 --> 07:32.666
I-I was going to ask for help!

07:32.917 --> 07:34.501
Josuke! Okuyasu!

07:35.836 --> 07:37.712
See you guys at school in a bit!

07:37.797 --> 07:38.589
Yeah!

07:38.673 --> 07:39.965
Don't be late.

07:40.049 --> 07:41.091
Got it!

07:43.552 --> 07:45.554
N-No!

07:45.846 --> 07:49.099
That's not what I wanted to say!

07:47.348 --> 07:49.141
I CANNOT ATTACK
THE MANGA ARTIST, ROHAN KISHIBE

07:49.225 --> 07:52.561
CANNOT

07:52.937 --> 07:55.856
Damn! I'm not
able to ask them for help.

07:58.526 --> 08:01.612
This Stand is beyond terrifying!

08:02.029 --> 08:05.741
Heaven's Door is unshakable!
It's invincible!

08:08.995 --> 08:10.413
Ah, I see…

08:12.623 --> 08:16.877
<i>At this rate, he's going to rip
everything out of me and kill me!</i>

08:20.047 --> 08:22.257
Someone's entered the mansion!

08:22.550 --> 08:25.177
What did you do downstairs, Koichi?

08:25.386 --> 08:26.428
Huh?

08:32.560 --> 08:33.602
Okuyasu!

08:34.562 --> 08:38.023
Hold it right there!
Just keep looking straight ahead.

08:38.149 --> 08:40.151
Don't try anything,

08:40.234 --> 08:42.611
or I'll crush you with my Stand,
you doodling s.o.b.

08:42.695 --> 08:43.612
Okuyasu!

08:44.071 --> 08:48.571
I don't know how you knew
I was in danger, but I'm ecstatic!

08:49.368 --> 08:52.579
It appears you've had an epiphany.

08:53.122 --> 08:56.500
I hadn't noticed before,
but that little wound on your hand

08:56.584 --> 08:58.961
must've given away
your little predicament.

08:59.920 --> 09:01.796
I suppose you scratched it
or caught it on something

09:01.881 --> 09:03.173
while you were crawling.

09:03.758 --> 09:05.801
I-I was so entranced,
I didn't notice…

09:06.469 --> 09:09.555
That's what gave it away,
right, Okuyasu Nijimura?

09:09.930 --> 09:11.681
Stand name: The Hand…

09:12.475 --> 09:15.811
You have a complex about
your dead brother, Keicho,

09:16.187 --> 09:18.314
and whenever you try to
make a decision,

09:18.564 --> 09:22.651
you wish that
your brother were there.

09:23.652 --> 09:24.402
Wha…

09:24.612 --> 09:27.615
What? Who the hell are you?

09:27.698 --> 09:31.034
Hey, Koichi, tell me what
this guy's Stand is!

09:31.118 --> 09:32.661
W-Well…

09:33.162 --> 09:35.038
<i>I-I can't!</i>

09:35.122 --> 09:38.041
<i>I can't say anything that would put
Rohan Kishibe at a disadvantage.</i>

09:38.334 --> 09:40.336
<i>One look at a single panel,
and it's all over!</i>

09:40.503 --> 09:43.714
<i>I desperately want to tell you…
don't look!</i>

09:43.798 --> 09:45.841
<i>Don't look at that manga!</i>

09:46.634 --> 09:49.678
Hey, I said don't move!

09:50.596 --> 09:53.640
Okuyasu, you were of
no concern to me,

09:53.891 --> 09:56.310
but all of that changed
when you set foot in this house.

09:56.811 --> 09:59.271
I'll have to turn you
into an inspiration, too.

10:00.648 --> 10:02.733
You bastard!

10:06.112 --> 10:06.779
What?!

10:06.862 --> 10:07.863
H-He's fast!

10:12.827 --> 10:14.453
Okuyasu!

10:16.622 --> 10:18.457
What the hell is this?!

10:18.541 --> 10:19.959
Josuke Higashikata,

10:21.168 --> 10:22.627
I know you're hiding over there.

10:29.385 --> 10:32.054
HEAVEN'S DOOR

10:34.682 --> 10:35.724
Okuyasu!

10:36.058 --> 10:38.560
What the hell is up
with this manga freak?

10:38.727 --> 10:40.186
Oh, be quiet.

10:41.397 --> 10:45.150
Now, then… Koichi,
I have a question.

10:45.234 --> 10:45.984
Huh?

10:46.193 --> 10:48.195
Why do you think Josuke Higashikata

10:48.404 --> 10:50.406
is hiding behind that door?

10:52.324 --> 10:54.159
Well? What do you think?

10:54.451 --> 10:56.619
Why won't he show himself, Koichi?

10:57.997 --> 11:02.497
Josuke is hiding so
he won't catch sight of your manga.

11:03.252 --> 11:06.296
Indeed, right on the money.
How very astute of you.

11:07.173 --> 11:11.510
Okuyasu Nijimura knew
nothing about my Heaven's Door,

11:11.594 --> 11:13.178
so he fell right into my trap.

11:14.054 --> 11:17.640
Conversely, his ignorance
exposed to Josuke Higashikata

11:17.725 --> 11:19.309
the workings of my Stand.

11:19.935 --> 11:21.394
At this point, I can't help
but feel I'm at somewhat,

11:21.478 --> 11:25.315
no, I'm at a significant
disadvantage.

11:26.066 --> 11:30.566
But Josuke Higashikata has
another reason for his concealment.

11:31.739 --> 11:33.240
What do you think that is?

11:34.491 --> 11:37.660
So that this no longer continues,

11:37.786 --> 11:38.995
I will have to resort to something

11:39.079 --> 11:41.372
in order to smoke him out
of his hiding place.

11:41.832 --> 11:45.293
He's busy figuring out
how to massacre you!

11:46.462 --> 11:47.796
That's also correct.

11:48.464 --> 11:50.549
But that's not the exact answer
I was looking for.

11:51.800 --> 11:53.468
The answer I want is…

11:54.094 --> 11:57.847
Josuke Higashikata
is contemplating whether

11:57.932 --> 12:00.726
he should flee this mansion
all by his lonesome.

12:00.935 --> 12:03.103
Josuke would never do that!

12:03.312 --> 12:04.730
Right, Koichi.

12:05.648 --> 12:09.318
Your files tell me that it is in
Josuke Higashikata's character

12:09.401 --> 12:11.736
to never abandon you two.

12:12.446 --> 12:15.657
But, the manga artist tends to,
on account of his work,

12:15.824 --> 12:20.324
consider every conceivable possibility
at every conceivable moment.

12:21.080 --> 12:23.373
In this situation,
with this protagonist,

12:23.457 --> 12:25.917
what would he or she do?

12:26.502 --> 12:31.002
In this case, Josuke fleeing
with knowledge of my Stand

12:31.257 --> 12:32.883
would put me in quite the catch-22.

12:33.259 --> 12:36.553
Run… That's not a bad idea.

12:36.637 --> 12:38.388
He could go get Jotaro,

12:38.472 --> 12:40.474
and if Yukako found out
what's happened to you,

12:40.557 --> 12:42.392
she'd be enraged.

12:42.476 --> 12:44.686
Ah! She'd beat him with her hair!

12:44.770 --> 12:45.854
Though I really don't
want to see her again!

12:45.938 --> 12:48.982
Come on, Josuke!
Hurry up and let them know!

12:49.066 --> 12:50.317
You fools!

12:50.401 --> 12:53.362
I explained that to you exactly
so it wouldn't happen!

12:53.445 --> 12:56.656
Okuyasu! I already wrote that
into your body!

12:56.907 --> 12:57.908
Huh?

12:58.033 --> 13:02.533
I give you permission to explain
the content of my missive, Koichi.

13:06.583 --> 13:07.584
No!

13:08.502 --> 13:10.295
What'd he write, Koichi?

13:10.379 --> 13:13.340
B-But that's… No…

13:13.549 --> 13:15.968
We're completely trapped!

13:16.385 --> 13:19.262
There's no running from this!

13:19.346 --> 13:22.891
That's why I'm asking you
what he wrote, Koichi!

13:22.891 --> 13:26.811
IF JOSUKE HIGASHIKATA CAUSES
TROUBLE FOR ROHAN KISHIBE,
I WILL BURN MYSELF TO DEATH

13:28.605 --> 13:30.398
B-Burn myself to death?!

13:30.691 --> 13:35.191
You'll kill yourself if Josuke
so much as tries to help us!

13:37.990 --> 13:41.118
H-Hey, hey! I burn myself to death?

13:42.244 --> 13:46.706
That's crazy talk! Like I'd ever do
something so horrible to myself!

13:47.541 --> 13:48.291
Huh?

13:48.417 --> 13:50.502
You will! He's invincible!

13:50.878 --> 13:53.213
We're completely incapable
of defying him!

13:53.297 --> 13:55.590
Stop! My right hand!

14:01.638 --> 14:02.764
You decided to join us.

14:03.015 --> 14:04.391
I don't think he
decided anything…

14:04.475 --> 14:07.561
Something dragged him out here.

14:08.937 --> 14:11.272
Ah… Rather a childish
and simple-minded move,

14:11.357 --> 14:13.400
but potentially effective as well.

14:13.734 --> 14:15.318
There's nowhere to run
in this cramped room.

14:15.694 --> 14:17.237
One knockout blow to me,

14:17.321 --> 14:18.655
and Heaven's Door
will release its grip,

14:18.739 --> 14:20.949
and Okuyasu won't commit suicide.

14:22.409 --> 14:23.451
Josuke!

14:26.246 --> 14:29.207
<i>Closing his eyes is simple-minded,
but it just might work.</i>

14:29.291 --> 14:30.542
<i>As long as he doesn't
see the manuscript,</i>

14:30.626 --> 14:32.127
<i>Heaven's Door is powerless.</i>

14:32.211 --> 14:33.795
<i>Keep coming… straight ahead!</i>

14:35.255 --> 14:36.130
Which means…

14:36.507 --> 14:40.636
All I have to do is get you
to open your eyes somehow.

14:45.140 --> 14:47.350
Oh! He's standing firm.

14:47.476 --> 14:48.477
Bad news…

14:48.602 --> 14:51.813
If he keeps charging at
me like that, all bets will be off.

14:51.980 --> 14:56.480
SECONDS

14:52.106 --> 14:55.609
<i>If I were a manga protagonist,
what would I do?</i>

14:55.818 --> 14:57.861
<i>How would I get him
to open his eyes?</i>

14:58.946 --> 15:00.697
Go, Josuke!

15:00.781 --> 15:02.616
Hurry up, Josuke!

15:03.367 --> 15:04.117
That's it!

15:04.201 --> 15:06.328
Something in Koichi's file…

15:07.454 --> 15:09.289
There! This is it!

15:10.582 --> 15:14.836
Comments like,
"Your hair makes me laugh, Josuke!"

15:15.087 --> 15:18.590
Or, "Wasn't that on trend, like,
twenty or thirty years ago?"

15:18.924 --> 15:21.635
And, "You think you look cool?"

15:22.052 --> 15:23.053
Like that, right?

15:24.596 --> 15:27.307
I guess that's what sets him off.

15:27.933 --> 15:31.978
Inconceivable, yes,
but the files do not lie.

15:32.146 --> 15:34.189
It's 100% true.

15:37.151 --> 15:40.112
What did you just say?

15:40.654 --> 15:42.739
J-Josuke, settle down!

15:43.157 --> 15:45.284
Why don't you try
and say that again!

15:45.492 --> 15:46.659
There they are…

15:47.536 --> 15:49.287
Didn't you hear me?

15:49.413 --> 15:53.875
You may think that hair looks cool,

15:54.334 --> 15:56.627
but on you it looks like shit.

15:56.837 --> 15:57.587
Lame!

15:58.464 --> 16:02.964
Though that noggin of yours may make
a disgusting pigeon very happy.

16:04.887 --> 16:06.597
That's a strong "may," though.

16:13.437 --> 16:14.855
Heaven's Door!

16:17.941 --> 16:18.942
<i>I win.</i>

16:20.569 --> 16:21.570
Huh?!

16:23.155 --> 16:23.905
What?!

16:32.331 --> 16:34.416
W-What the hell?

16:34.708 --> 16:39.208
I-I know I opened his eyes
and showed him the manuscript!

16:46.053 --> 16:47.721
W-We're back to normal!

16:50.265 --> 16:53.268
But I showed it to him… Why?

16:54.686 --> 16:57.355
Now where the hell'd
you stuff off to?!

16:58.398 --> 17:00.441
Get back out here, goddammit!

17:01.276 --> 17:03.736
He's not really seeing…

17:03.946 --> 17:05.155
He's not really seeing?

17:05.239 --> 17:07.866
You mean he's so worked up,

17:08.158 --> 17:10.451
he doesn't even know
what he's doing?

17:11.912 --> 17:14.581
Where are you,
you manga-obsessed asshole?!

17:14.665 --> 17:15.749
Get out here!

17:15.916 --> 17:18.585
Yeah… Any kind of hair insult,

17:18.669 --> 17:21.004
it doesn't matter if it's from
a comic or someone's mouth,

17:21.088 --> 17:23.298
he flies into a blind rage.

17:25.884 --> 17:29.679
I had no idea he had such a temper.

17:30.055 --> 17:32.849
It's beyond my wildest imagination.

17:33.141 --> 17:34.642
What?

17:38.772 --> 17:41.024
There was a facet of
Josuke's personality

17:41.108 --> 17:42.859
that even Koichi didn't know?

17:43.110 --> 17:46.154
That means it wasn't
written in the file!

17:46.280 --> 17:50.575
Why? Why does he get
so mad over his hair?

17:50.951 --> 17:54.371
There has to be a reason… Why?

17:54.997 --> 17:57.040
I show no mercy!

17:57.457 --> 18:00.293
I won't take that bullshit
from anyone!

18:00.627 --> 18:01.753
The reason…

18:01.962 --> 18:04.923
I think I may've heard it before.

18:05.132 --> 18:07.509
That just might be why…

18:07.801 --> 18:09.636
Huh? What are you talking about?

18:10.220 --> 18:13.848
It was when Josuke
was a kid, but…

18:16.143 --> 18:19.146
I'll try and remember
the story as best I can,

18:19.229 --> 18:21.314
I might have to fill in some gaps.

18:25.152 --> 18:27.028
Josuke was four,

18:27.195 --> 18:29.614
and he had passed out from
an inexplicably high fever.

18:30.032 --> 18:33.326
For fifty days, he was within
a hair's breadth of death.

18:34.328 --> 18:35.203
<i>Josuke…</i>

18:38.707 --> 18:41.543
He found out later that it was
right around the time

18:41.627 --> 18:43.211
Jotaro and Mr. Joestar

18:43.420 --> 18:47.215
traveled to Egypt to
defeat the man named DIO.

18:47.924 --> 18:50.301
With no idea what was happening,

18:50.594 --> 18:54.723
Josuke's mom headed to
a hospital in S City.

18:55.307 --> 18:59.394
But Morioh was in the middle
of its worst blizzard in 18 years.

19:00.562 --> 19:02.730
<i>It's no use… What should I do?</i>

19:05.734 --> 19:08.737
<i>Nobody ever drives around here,</i>

19:09.112 --> 19:10.404
<i>and there's not
a payphone in sight.</i>

19:11.198 --> 19:14.242
<i>I should've called
an ambulance from the house.</i>

19:14.493 --> 19:17.913
<i>I shouldn't have brought
Josuke out in this snow.</i>

19:19.831 --> 19:20.915
That's when it happened.

19:28.340 --> 19:31.384
<i>W-What do you want? Go away!</i>

19:36.223 --> 19:39.267
YOUR KID IS SICK, RIGHT?
I'll PUSH YOUR CAR.

19:39.393 --> 19:40.560
<i>Huh?</i>

19:48.860 --> 19:51.112
NOW STEP ON THE GAS.

19:52.447 --> 19:56.451
ONCE YOU GAIN TRACTION,
DON'T STOP. JUST GUN IT…
OR YOU'LL GET STUCK AGAIN.

19:57.577 --> 19:59.078
<i>Got it…</i>

20:16.096 --> 20:17.180
<i>Thank you!</i>

20:27.149 --> 20:29.693
His mom eventually
tried to search for the young man,

20:30.235 --> 20:32.111
but found no information.

20:32.863 --> 20:37.363
That young man may've not
personally saved his life,

20:38.160 --> 20:41.163
but in the eyes of
four-year-old Josuke,

20:41.455 --> 20:42.956
he was his hero.

20:43.874 --> 20:46.459
He became a permanent inspiration,

20:46.668 --> 20:48.336
his role model for life.

20:49.171 --> 20:50.589
An affront to that part of him,

20:51.006 --> 20:53.633
triggers something
deep in his heart.

20:54.426 --> 20:56.678
<i>I don't know who he is
or where he's from,</i>

20:57.637 --> 21:00.681
<i>but as a tribute to him,
I adopted the same hairstyle.</i>

21:01.641 --> 21:03.225
<i>I won't put up with
anyone who disrespects it,</i>

21:03.310 --> 21:04.602
<i>I don't care who it is.</i>

21:04.770 --> 21:07.689
<i>It's disrespectful to him.</i>

21:08.648 --> 21:11.525
That has to be the reason.

21:11.818 --> 21:13.611
I thought Josuke
was just making it up,

21:13.695 --> 21:15.905
so I wasn't listening
very carefully.

21:16.323 --> 21:18.408
Huh… I had no idea.

21:21.036 --> 21:22.704
Rohan's holding a pen!

21:22.954 --> 21:25.039
Bastard! At it again, huh?!

21:25.123 --> 21:26.124
N-No…

21:26.208 --> 21:30.708
I-I wanted to jot this all down
before I lost consciousness.

21:31.046 --> 21:32.589
What a magnificent story!

21:33.006 --> 21:36.175
And I just had
an amazing experience.

21:36.343 --> 21:37.510
I'm elated.

21:37.636 --> 21:40.555
Experiences like that are rare.

21:40.680 --> 21:42.306
If I can just incorporate it
into my own work…

21:43.642 --> 21:44.934
I'm so blessed.

21:45.018 --> 21:47.812
I'm so glad I moved to Morioh.

21:47.938 --> 21:49.314
It's no use.

21:49.481 --> 21:51.608
As long as he's alive, he won't stop
searching for manga material,

21:51.691 --> 21:53.526
no matter how
horrible the experience.

21:53.860 --> 21:56.654
At this point,
you have to commend him.

21:56.738 --> 22:01.238
Good and bad aside,
I have to admire his outlook.

22:01.785 --> 22:04.370
He's truly a super manga artist.

22:04.996 --> 22:07.289
There you are, manga artist!

22:07.666 --> 22:09.834
I'm not done punching you!

22:11.586 --> 22:14.422
I think ya have to
commend him, too.

22:14.631 --> 22:15.840
Y-Yeah…

22:19.469 --> 22:23.969
ROHAN KISHIBE'S
PINK DARK BOY
— SUSPENSION NOTICE —
SORRY!
THANK YOU FOR YOUR CONTINUED
READERSHIP OF PINK DARK BOY.
DUE TO PERSONAL MATTERS,
OUR PUBLICATION WILL BE
SUSPENDED FOR ONE MONTH.
(FROM THE EDITORS)

22:20.554 --> 22:23.431
<i>Rohan Kishibe's</i> Pink Dark Boy

22:23.723 --> 22:25.933
<i>will be suspended
for one month.</i>

23:38.632 --> 23:41.509
EPISODE 16
LET'S GO HUNTING!
